The four hypotheses for salinity origins in northeastern Guanabara Bay are:  
1) Recharge zones near the basin headboard or connected to fractured basement aquifers (low Cl/Br ratio, light δ¹⁸O and δ²H);  
2) Groundwater with high Cl/Br ratio and heavy δ¹⁸O and δ²H, linked to dissolution of Tertiary brackish sediments;  
3) Groundwater derived from low-salinity recharge areas with specific isotopic signatures;  
4) Groundwater influenced by evaporation and mixing processes in coastal zones.  

[Citation: PIRA-DOC-3ff4936e693d541b-C001 and PIRA-DOC-4db48
